Source: kiremote
Section: net
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Kiyoshi Spreclerg <kiyoshi_pip@protonmail.com>
# kidesktop-core is here for the headers the panel widget and the popup page
# are built against (xispanel_widget.h, xisserve_page.h): it installs them.
# The "~" lets its own per-distro versions (0.1.4~ubuntu22.04) count.
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13),
               pkg-config,
               gettext,
               libssl-dev,
               libdbus-1-dev,
               libx11-dev,
               libxfixes-dev,
               libxtst-dev,
               libxext-dev,
               libgtk2.0-dev,
               libcairo2-dev,
               kidesktop-core (>= 0.1.4~)
Standards-Version: 4.6.0
Homepage: https://github.com/kiyoshispreclerg/kiremote
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: kiremote
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends},
         ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: kiremote-gtk | kiremote-kidesktop,
            pulseaudio-utils,
            sshfs,
            xdg-utils
Description: connects this computer to your phone (KDE Connect protocol)
 Kiremote's daemon and command line. It speaks protocol version 8 of KDE
 Connect, so the official KDE Connect app on the phone works with it, without
 Qt or KDE libraries on this side: pairing, ping, files, clipboard,
 notifications, battery and signal, finding the phone, media and volume
 control, remote mouse and keyboard, a presentation pointer, remote commands,
 locking the screen and browsing the phone's files.
 .
  * kiremoted - the daemon (starts with the session; no GUI, no threads)
  * kiremote-cli - controls it from the terminal and scripts
 .
 The phone finds this computer through UDP 1716 and TCP 1716-1764 on the
 local network. An interface is a separate package: kiremote-gtk for any
 desktop, kiremote-kidesktop for KiDesktop.

Package: kiremote-gtk
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends},
         ${misc:Depends},
         kiremote (= ${binary:Version})
Recommends: adwaita-icon-theme | gnome-icon-theme
Description: Kiremote window and tray icon for any desktop (GTK 2)
 The Kiremote interface for desktops that are not KiDesktop: a window with
 the phones around (battery, signal, ping, find, send files and text, browse,
 pair and unpair), the pairing question with the verification key, and every
 setting, plus a tray icon. Only one window runs per session.
 .
 It has to be running to hear a pairing request, so the package starts it
 hidden with the session.

Package: kiremote-kidesktop
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends},
         ${misc:Depends},
         kiremote (= ${binary:Version}),
         kidesktop-core (>= 0.1.4~),
         libgtk2.0-0
Enhances: kidesktop-core
Description: Kiremote for KiDesktop: panel widget, popup page and settings tab
 The Kiremote interface integrated into KiDesktop, with the same functions
 and settings as kiremote-gtk:
 .
  * a kiconf tab with all the settings
  * an xisserve page (xisserve --kiremote): the devices with battery and
    signal, an actions menu on each, pair and unpair
  * an xispanel widget (WIDGET ... kiremote): the phone icon with the number
    of connected devices; it also asks the pairing questions, through
    xisserve --question
 .
 Add the widget to a panel in kiconf (Panels) or in xispanel.conf.
